{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nc6pwNsTyNDK2LJTDXLGvp","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519/projects/nlp_variance_gtheory/decisions.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"_next_id: 6\\\\ndecisions:\\\\n- id: D001\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 18:57 UTC\\\\n  summary: MVP PASS — G-theory 方差分解在 LLM 评估中可行，item 方差主导（58.4%），separability 在聚合层面成立，进入\\\\n    research 阶段\\\\n  rationale: 5,400 次推理完成，5 个方差分量 ≥5% 且 CI 不含零，pipeline 端到端可运行。核心发现：(1) item 选择是评估方差最大来源；(2)\\\\n    precision/temperature/prompt 效应是 item-specific 的；(3) 直接的 infrastructure×methodology\\\\n    交互可忽略（<0.02%）。float32 引擎混淆需全研究阶段解决但不影响 MVP 结论。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on: []\\\\n- id: D002\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 19:12 UTC\\\\n  summary: 采用 dual-metric (binary correct + text exact match) 方差分解作为论文核心方法论，Claim\\\\n    3 改为 metric-conditional reproducibility budget\\\\n  rationale: MVP 双变量分析揭示截然不同的方差结构：binary correct 下 item_id 主导 (58.4%, G=0.357)；text\\\\n    exact match 下 prompt×item 主导 (37.5%, G=0.975)。单一 response variable 无法完整描述评估可靠性。Dual-metric\\\\n    对比是 G-theory 框架的天然优势——\\\\\\\"同一实验在不同衡量标准下可靠性完全不同\\\\\\\"是比单一 budget 更有力的发现。precision:temperature\\\\n    交互在 text metric 下显著 (1.3%, CI 不含零)，证明 separability 在细粒度下不完全成立。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D001\\\\n- id: D003\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 22:20 UTC\\\\n  summary: Dream 审稿后调整 framing：infrastructure crossing 降级为 confirmatory，cross-benchmark\\\\n    gradient 升级为 primary novelty，model-as-facet 加入分析计划\\\\n  rationale: Dream full review (dream_20260520T190053) 三档评分：Best 3/6, Median 4/6,\\\\n    Worst 3/6。三档一致暴露 9 个结构性问题：(1) bibliography 严重不足（需 25+ refs）; (2) model 未作为 G-theory\\\\n    facet（inflates item_id）; (3) 无 bootstrap CIs; (4) 零 figures; (5) infrastructure\\\\n    crossing 为 confirmatory null 非 breakthrough; (6) item dominance 心理测量学预期，oversold;\\\\n    (7) \\\\\\\"fully crossed\\\\\\\" 过度声称; (8) \\\\\\\"diagnostic tool\\\\\\\" 无实质; (9) fine-tuning 用 RoBERTa\\\\n    距离太远。全部为 framing/分析问题，不影响实验设计——P0 实验不变，但 framing 需大改，exp-004 分析内容扩展。需 re-dream\\\\n    验证后批准 P0。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-001\\\\n    role: unchanged\\\\n    result: design not affected by framing changes\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-004\\\\n    role: expanded\\\\n    result: added model-as-facet, bootstrap CIs, higher-order interactions, IRT comparison\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D001\\\\n  - D002\\\\n- id: D004\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 00:08 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'Re-dream #2 通过质量门控（Best 4/6, Median 4/6），批准 exp-001 启动'\\\\n  rationale: 'Dream #2 评分：Best 4/6 (Weak Accept), Median 4/6 (Weak Accept), Worst\\\\n    3/6 (Weak Reject)。Best ≥ weak accept 且 Median ≥ borderline，满足 post-MVP kickoff\\\\n    Step 5 的批准条件。相比 Dream #1 (3/4/3)，Best 从 3→4 提升，结构性问题已解决。剩余问题均为分析/呈现层面：(1) 零 figures\\\\n    — 论文写作阶段处理; (2) D-study 优化过程需文档化 — exp-004; (3) Bootstrap 重采样独立性问题 — 加 jackknife\\\\n    对比到 exp-004; (4) G 系数解读需区分 item-level 与 benchmark-level — 论文 Discussion; (5) Cross-benchmark\\\\n    设计不对称需 sensitivity analysis — exp-004; (6) IRT 对比 — 已纳入 exp-004; (7) Exp 5/6/7\\\\n    建议移至 appendix — 论文写作。所有剩余问题不影响 exp-001 实验设计。'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-001\\\\n    role: approved\\\\n    result: re-dream passes, proceed with full-scale experiment\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D003\\\\n- id: D005\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 02:26 UTC\\\\n  summary: Gemma2 fp16 不可用 — cross-model 分析用 bf16+fp32 平衡设计，fp16 仅用于 within-model\\\\n  rationale: vLLM 报告 Gemma2 架构不支持 fp16（numerical instability）。bf16 vs fp16 差异 <0.1pp（Llama\\\\n    数据），precision 信号集中在 fp32 vs 其他（10.7pp）。cross-model 用 2 precisions 不损失 power，fp16\\\\n    数据在 Llama/Mistral/Qwen within-model 分析中保留。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-001\\\\n    role: affected\\\\n    result: Gemma fp16 conditions marked N/A, cross-model analysis scoped to bf16+fp32\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D004\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 3318, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NfSvsAu7kWLukJQcn5o4jF","session_id":"61758983-af28-4ed0-aeee-c7c8e76b89a4","uuid":"9234c83b-63b2-4a21-97d0-1b95ae9a8557","timestamp":"2026-05-21T06:03:21.518Z"}
